{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.RouteCPivotalVsCount","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.RouteCPivotalVsCount","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.RouteCPivotalVsCount.ordinary_partial_trace_scalar_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.RouteCPivotalVsCount.ordinary_partial_trace_scalar_iff","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/RouteCPivotalVsCount.lean#L87-L105","doc":"The unweighted partial trace of the R-matrix over the closed strand is\n`diag(2q − q⁻¹, q)` (computed in the probe); it is scalar iff its two diagonal\nentries agree, i.e. iff `q² = 1`.  This is the step that makes the ordinary\ntrace fail the Markov property away from `q = ±1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.RouteCPivotalVsCount.zJ_eq_zD_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.RouteCPivotalVsCount.zJ_eq_zD_iff","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/RouteCPivotalVsCount.lean#L70-L85","doc":"The two parameters coincide iff `q² = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.RouteCPivotalVsCount.zJ_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.RouteCPivotalVsCount.zJ_one","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/RouteCPivotalVsCount.lean#L65-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.RouteCPivotalVsCount.zD_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.RouteCPivotalVsCount.zD_one","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/RouteCPivotalVsCount.lean#L61-L63","doc":"Both parameters are `1/2` at `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.RouteCPivotalVsCount.zJ_sub_zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.RouteCPivotalVsCount.zJ_sub_zD","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/RouteCPivotalVsCount.lean#L53-L59","doc":"The exact difference: a double root at `q = 1` (and at `q = −1`), so the two\nparameters share value and slope there and part at second order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.RouteCPivotalVsCount.zJ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.RouteCPivotalVsCount.zJ","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/RouteCPivotalVsCount.lean#L50-L51","doc":"Ordinary-trace (count-shaped) Markov parameter on spin-½: `(3q − q⁻¹) / 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.RouteCPivotalVsCount.zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.RouteCPivotalVsCount.zD","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/RouteCPivotalVsCount.lean#L47-L48","doc":"Convention-D (pivotal) Markov parameter on spin-½: `q³ / (q² + 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}